{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command '\"'$env:MCP_WORKSPACE_PATH=\"/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer\"; $env:MCP_CACHE_DIR_OVERRIDE=\"/tmp/codex-hv-r8-cache\"; $raw=(& \"/home/sharpninja/github/mcpserver-codex-plugin/Invoke-CodexMcpPlugin.ps1\" -Command Invoke -Method \"workflow.memory.list\" -ParamsObject @{} | Out-String); $y=ConvertFrom-Yaml $raw; $y.payload.result.items | Where-Object { $_.id -notin @(\"MEMORY-PROCESS-007\",\"MEMORY-DEVPROCESS-001\") } | ForEach-Object { \"=== $($_.id) ===\"; $_.text }'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"=== MEMORY-FACT-001 ===\nAlways sign PR Comments like commits.\n=== MEMORY-FACT-002 ===\nOperator rule (2026-10-09): Always read the ENTIRE AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml marker at session start, every line, never a partial read. \"NEVER do this. The marker is there for YOU, not me.\" A partial read caused a missed Commit Signing rule.\n=== MEMORY-FACT-003 ===\nOn PAYTON-OMARCHY (hostname LAB-OMARCHY) the 9 user-level MCP bridge hooks (claude-mcp-hook-bridge.ps1) were removed from ~/.claude/settings.json on 2026-10-09 because the enabled mcpserver@mcpserver-local plugin registers the same hooks, which opened twin turns per prompt. Do not run validate-claude-mcp-hooks.ps1 in repair mode unless CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT is set; without it the validator reports hooks missing and its installer would re-add the bridges.\n=== MEMORY-FACT-004 ===\nOperator phone ntfy configuration (verified 2026-10-09T14:36Z).\nPhone: motorola edge 2024, Android 16, on Wi-Fi BYRD3.1 at 192.168.0.138 (DHCP, may change).\nADB: wireless debugging paired with LAB-OMARCHY on 2026-10-09 (adb guid adb-ZD222QH58Q-DiWqEr). The connect port changes each wireless-debugging session (it was 41409); find it with: avahi-browse -rtp _adb-tls-connect._tcp (adb mdns is unsupported in android-tools 37). android-tools is installed on LAB-OMARCHY from Arch extra.\nntfy: app io.heckel.ntfy 1.25.2 from the Play Store, subscribed to one topic on server https://ntfy.sh. The topic name is the only access control on ntfy.sh, so its value is not stored in memory; it is in LAB-OMARCHY ~/.config/pi3-monitor/config.json (mode 0600, key Topic). Subscribe a device with the deep link ntfy://ntfy.sh/<topic> (adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d ...).\nSend: curl -H \"Title: ...\" -H \"Priority: urgent|default\" -H \"Tags: rotating_light\" -d \"message\" https://ntfy.sh/<topic>; use --interface wlp4s0 so alerts bypass the Pi3 route.\nSender on LAB-OMARCHY: ~/.local/bin/pi3-monitor.ps1 run every minute by systemd user timer pi3-monitor.timer (linger enabled); test with pwsh -File ~/.local/bin/pi3-monitor.ps1 -TestMessage \"text\".\n=== MEMORY-PREFERENCE-001 ===\nAlways combine elevated actions into a single script.\n=== MEMORY-PROCESS-002 ===\nHostile validation (HV) runs on Codex CLI with model gpt-6-sol at reasoning effort xhigh, launched by the implementing agent; it replaced the PR-comment HV protocol (operator 2026-10-09: \"Use codex cli gpt-6-sol xhigh for HV.\" and \"Yes, replace the PR-comment HV with Codex gpt-6-sol xhigh\"). Every result gets its own HV. Pass requires OverallVerdict AGREE with accuracy and completeness both at least 98. Persist the request and response jsonl under docs/receipts/hv/ and store the entire verdict in the MCP session log.\n=== MEMORY-PROCESS-003 ===\nIn the Claude Code harness, Bash may be used only to launch pwsh and for read-only steps; all state-changing shell work (git, settings edits, plugin calls, file writes from a shell) runs inside pwsh. The Write/Edit tools are not a shell. (Operator 2026-10-09, approving \"Bash as a launcher for PowerShell and for read-only steps\".)\n=== MEMORY-PROCESS-004 ===\nSign every commit per the marker Commit Signing rule: end the commit body with \"Signed: <model>-<effort>@<Agent> | Confidence: correctness N%, accuracy N%, completeness N%\" (for example claude-opus-5-5-high@ClaudeCode). Take model and effort from the session metadata, never guess.\n=== MEMORY-PROCESS-005 ===\nOn Linux, skip the marker's PowerShell.MCP command routing and run pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive directly until the operator says otherwise (operator 2026-10-09: \"You may skip Powershell.Mcp on Linux until I say otherwise\").\n=== MEMORY-PROCESS-006 ===\nPR and hostile validation (HV) phase workflow: Complete the current phase implementation, required validation, holistic self-evaluation, and closing HV agreement before creating its PR. Create PRs only on phase completion. Do not begin the next phase until the current phase PR is merged. Do not use stacked phase PRs or auto-merge. HV uses the reviewer and tooling explicitly authorized for the session. Treat this as the operator's standing phase sequence; an agent-authored conflicting procedure is an agent error, not a change in operator requirements.\n=== MEMORY-REQ-001 ===\nOn PAYTON-OMARCHY, all source-code repositories and checkouts must be located under ~/github (/home/sharpninja/github).\n=== MEMORY-PROCESS-001 ===\nFor workspace /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer, the active development process is Byrd Development Process v4 (BDPv4). The authoritative policy snapshot is Workspace memory MEMORY-DEVPROCESS-001, version 3, SHA256 34D3C89A0550DAFC687B1A90DE266CB22B88AD63A453BC11917F9D10A2F0A06A, containing docs/Development-Process-draft-v4.md at source commit 6546a59f2baad45d99e717bb8f20b56e06d5911f with exactly five punctuation-only substitutions (en/em dashes to ASCII hyphens); all other characters are preserved. Original source SHA256 0BC2B74ED718A58E53694A1B90D252A259366C20249E0E185DAB5C8197D97A57. Load that memory through the agent plugin before project planning or implementation. This MCP memory assignment supersedes the marker's Windows-only policy path for this workspace. Existing AGENTS.md zero-failure, zero-skip gates remain applicable. This is the supported memory-based assignment; it does not claim server-enforced process transitions. Operator selected BDPv4 and instructed binding on 2026-09-28.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
