: - opencode: turn opens in `chat.message` for user messages with nonce `messageID` (fired when the message is created, which is arrival); host session key `sessionID`; plugin tools read `_context.sessionID`, and shell commands get `MCP_HOST_SESSION_KEY` from the `shell.env` hook; stop-equivalent `session.idle`; the start/end regexes and the factory signature are replaced.\n 91: \n 92: P0 per plugin: fetch origin; resolve the remote default branch with `git ls-remote --symref origin HEAD` (`main` for eight repos, `master` for opencode on 2026-10-09); compare local uncommitted work against origin lineage (`CORE-MANIFEST.yaml` coreVersion ancestry, EOL-insensitive diff); preserve any local work in a uniquely tagged stash (record SHA); fast-forward to that default branch; record version and head; re-check every row of the host binding table against the head and record any difference as a RequirementRefined decision before A1. Never discard uncommitted work without that receipt.\n 93: \n 94: Per-plugin changes:\n 95: - PowerShell hosts (claude-code, claude-cowork, codex, copilot, grok, grok-bot): receive all plugin-core changes through `./build.ps1 SyncAgentPlugins --agent-plugin-parent /home/sharpninja/github` (A9 and S8) plus host wrappers from `hooks-templates/generate-wrappers.ps1`; host-specific glue exactly as the host binding table states (nonce source, hook and verb host-session keys, subagent and system-event markers, stop field); the A9 repairs named there (codex `hooks/hooks.json`, copilot hook path, cowork connector, grok camelCase reads, the core's `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` and `stop_hook_active` reads); duplicate-registration detection where the host can double-register hooks (A2 equivalent; Grok's default run of `~/.claude/settings.json` hooks included); skill/README docs for recordReview, requestClass, automatic binding with optional requestId override.\n 96: - TypeScript hosts (cline, cline-v2, opencode): all shared behavior changes land once in `plugins/core/lib-node` (`src/tools/session.ts`, `src/tools/session-shim.ts`, `src/cache/cache-manager.ts`, `src/runtime/host-context.ts`, `src/transport/*`) in slices A8 and S9, with jest tests in `plugins/core/lib-node/tests` (`session-shim.test.ts`, `cache-manager.test.ts`, `host-context.test.ts`, `repl-bridge.test.ts`, plus new suites). Then each plugin adopts the new packed core and adds the host glue the host binding table fixes: cline-v2 (`beforeRun` mint with `runId`, `conversationId` key, `afterRun` stop-equivalent, no per-run session close, `@cline/core` pin raised), opencode (`chat.message` mint with `messageID`, `sessionID` key via `_context` and `shell.env`, `session.idle` stop-equivalent, regex and factory replaced), cline (Cline native UserPromptSubmit hook adapter with `taskId` key and derived nonce, MCP tools on the live-session rule, or `turn_logging_unsupported` per D6); each exposes `requestClass`, `session_record_review`, the `requestId` override (required under D9 while two or more delivered requests are open), truthful outcomes, decisions/requirements/blockers.\n 97: - Every plugin: version bump, `CORE-MANIFEST.yaml` or packed-core version pin (where applicable), plugin-owned docs/skills/ENFORCEMENT.md and their tests updated; marker `agent_plugins` versions verified after server restart.\n 98: \n 99: Per-plugin test gate (G6, run for every plugin touched by a slice; zero failures, zero skips):\n100: - PowerShell hosts: `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command \"Invoke-Pester -Path tests -CI\"` and `bats tests/*.bats`.\n101: - Node core: in `plugins/core/lib-node` `npm ci; npm run build; npm test` (jest), run on each of Node 18, 20, 22, and the latest release (D12 version matrix, through the version manager the host provides, for example `mise exec node@20 -- npm test`); the TypeScript hosts run their suites on their lowest declared engine and on the latest release.\n102: - TypeScript hosts (cline, cline-v2, opencode): `npm ci; npm run build; npm test` in each repo.\n103: - `./build.ps1 PluginSessionLogIntegration` for hosts it covers.\n104: - Phase exits require G6 green for all nine plugins and the Node core.\n105: \n106: ## Coordination with QB-AGENT-001 (Codex)\n107: \n108: Observed 2026-10-09T17:14Z (read-only): Codex is implementing QB-AGENT-001 in the McpServer worktree `/home/sharpninja/github/cline/.worktrees/mcpserver-qbrain`, branch `qb/p1-governance-core`, base `f56dcf70` (this plan's baseline), uncommitted, 10 modified and 8 new files, all under `plugins/core/lib-node` (`src/tools/session.ts`, `src/tools/session-shim.ts`, `src/runtime/host-context.ts`, `src/runtime/core-config.ts`, `src/transport/repl-bridge.ts`, `src/discovery/marker-resolver.ts`, `src/index.ts`; new `src/cache/audit-outbox.ts`, `src/runtime/core-runtime-error.ts`). Its relayed status: not merge-ready; P1 carries most McpServer changes; P2 adds paginated session-turn listing and detail reads; six-platform REPL packaging runs through P5. Two current designs conflict with this plan: `host-context.ts` refuses a second turn while one is open (`session_failed`, \"The current turn must finish before another starts\"), and the session tool enum adds an undocumented action type `tool_execution`.\n109: \n110: Channel (operator, 2026-10-09: \"I suggest using a single global mcp memory to act as a coms channel for coordination\"): Global MCP memory `MEMORY-PROCESS-007`, an append-only log with the protocol written in the memory itself (read, append one entry, write back, read back; KINDs NOTICE, REQUEST, ANSWER, CONTRACT, READINESS, ACK; READINESS carries commit SHA, PR, validation evidence, and the HV verdict; operator decisions are posted as REQUEST and never settled by an agent). The implementing agent reads it at session start and before every slice that touches a shared file.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
