nt, system-event classifier (lib-ps). AC-001 `turn-open.lock` serializes opens across processes in one workspace cache; AC-002 `Get-PluginIngressNonce -Host <host> -Payload <payload>` derives the nonce from the event exactly as the host binding table states for each hook host (a pure function: equal payloads give equal nonces), and when a payload lacks the field its host row names, the hook does not invent a nonce: it reports `turn-open-failed` with reason `nonce_source_missing` and writes a failsafe diagnostic, which the stop gate shows as warning `ingress_nonce_source_missing`; the nonce is written into the failsafe mint record before the first mint call; AC-003 classifier returns true exactly for the FR-002 event list; AC-004 hook-originated verbs carry `MCP_PLUGIN_HOOK_INVOCATION=1`; AC-005 `Invoke-PluginIngressMint` calls the server mint with the nonce, records the returned requestId (a prompt-hook mint is delivered at once, so it also becomes the host session's write target; a bridge mint stays `queued` until delivery), and on outage opens `pending-<nonce>` and rebinds it on drain; AC-006 `Start-PluginArrivalBridge` (claude-code, claude-cowork) is launched by SessionStart as a detached `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive` process with the workspace root as working directory, writes `sessions/<key>/arrival-bridge.pid`, tails `transcript_path` from `appliedThroughOffset`, applies each `queue-operation` record by the D5 lifecycle in the host binding table (mint at `enqueue`, deliver at `absorbed_mid_turn`, withdraw at other `remove` and `popAll`) to `turn-state.yaml` in one atomic replace that also advances `appliedThroughOffset`, skipping records that start below it, exits at SessionEnd or when its host session is ended, and a second start for the same key exits immediately; `Resolve-PluginBridgeClaim` lets the prompt hook claim a matching unclaimed bridge mint under `turn-open.lock`. [A3 +A5]\n341: - TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-002 Hook validator and installer (Claude plugin repo). AC-001 `Test-PluginEnabled` reads the `enabledPlugins` map and `known_marketplaces.json`; AC-002 `Get-DuplicateHookCommands` lists event:script duplicates; AC-003 validator JSON adds `duplicate`, `repaired`, `duplicateHooks`, `pluginEnabled`, `pluginKey`; AC-004 repair writes a backup and keeps non-MCP hooks. [A2]\n342: - TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003 Per-turn store, pointer, target resolution, stop ledger (lib-ps). AC-001 `turns/<requestId>.yaml` plus `.lock`; AC-002 `Resolve-ReplTargetTurn` contract (precedence: explicit requestId, else invocation binding; an unqualified verb is refused with `request_ambiguous` while two or more delivered requests are open, D9; an unknown explicit id is refused with `request_unknown`); AC-003 `Invoke-ReplSupersedeCurrentTurnIfInProgress` removed; AC-004 `stop-ledger.yaml` contract; AC-005 per-turn edits never overwrite another turn's title (absorbs the intent of retired TR-MCP-REPL-019); AC-006 `Get-PluginHostSessionKey` implements the host binding table (invocation-context key, else the live-session rule with `host_session_inferred`, `host_session_unknown`, `host_session_ambiguous`), and `New-ReplInvocationBinding` captures `{ hostSessionKey, keySource, requestId, boundAtUtc }` once per verb invocation into its persist and failsafe records; AC-007 `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/turn-state.yaml` is written only by the arrival bridge (mint, delivery, withdrawal, `appliedThroughOffset`), the prompt hook (claim, or mint and delivery), and the close verbs (removing a closed request from the open delivered list), each as one atomic replace under `turn-open.lock`; and `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/ended.yaml` only by the session-end hook or the 12-hour idle rule. [A4]\n343: - TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004 Server per-turn submit outcomes and ingress mint. AC-001 `ISessionLogService.SubmitWithOutcomesAsync`, `SubmitAsync` delegates; AC-002 `ISessionLogTurnUpsertGuard` seam replaces the inline guard at `SessionLogService.cs:1606-1618`; AC-003 `SessionLogSubmitResult.turns` on REST, MCP, client, REPL strategy; AC-004 decorators forward; AC-005 a new mint operation, because the existing begin route requires `{requestId}` in its path (`SessionLogController.cs:388-396`) and the client interpolates it (`SessionLogClient.cs:174-191`): REST `POST /qbrainai/sessionlog/{agent}/{sessionId}/mint` (the controller's second route attribute also serves it under `/mcpserver/sessionlog`, `SessionLogController.cs:15-16`) with body `SessionLogMintTurnRequest { ingressNonce (required, `^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]{1,64}$`), queryTitle, queryText, model, planFile (required; path or `None`), todoId (required; TODO id or `None`) }` validated like the begin body (`docs/context/session-log-schema.md:16,64-66`); responses 201 `{ requestId, outcome: \"created\" }`, 200 `{ requestId, outcome: \"merged\", storedStatus }` when the nonce already exists in that session, 400 `ingress_nonce_invalid` or the existing planFile/todoId validation errors, 404 when the session is not open; no MCP tool (the mint is not a model-visible tool; every `[McpServerTool]` in `FwhMcpTools.SessionLog.cs` is model-visible); client `MintTurnAsync(agent, sessionId, ingressNonce, queryTitle, queryText, model, planFile, todoId)`; REPL `workflow.sessionlog.mintTurn`, which the plugin wrappers refuse with `mint_requires_host_ingress` unless the call comes from a hook or adapter entry point (`MCP_PLUGIN_HOOK_INVOCATION=1`; a guard against accidental model use, not a security boundary) and which no model-facing skill or tool description mentions; the begin route and `BeginTurnAsync` keep today's behavior; AC-006 `SessionLogTurnEntity.IngressNonce` (string 64, nullable) with a unique filtered index on (WorkspaceId, SessionLogId, IngressNonce) where not null, added by migration `<utc>_AddSessionLogTurnIngressNonce` for SQLite, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server; a mint whose nonce exists returns the stored turn's requestId (unique-violation race resolved by re-read). [A1]\n344: - TR-MCP-SESSI