the 2026-10-09 inventory are in scope and fixed in A9 (see the matrix and host binding table), not filed separately.\n624: \n625: ## End-to-end verification\n626: \n627: - Phase A live check (after the A9 sync of all nine plugins, validator repair, restart): in a fresh Claude Code session send three prompts (two of them identical text, one queued mid-turn) and run one background agent; `client.SessionLog.QueryAsync` shows exactly three user turns with server-minted requestIds, none canceled, no `<task-notification>` turn, the queued message's turn minted at its enqueue time (turn creation within 2 seconds of the transcript `enqueue` timestamp), and every write of the work done after the queued message on the turn the D2 rule assigns; with R1 and R2 both delivered and open, an unqualified write is refused with `request_ambiguous` and the server shows zero writes from it, writes with explicit ids in the order R1, R2, R1 land on R1, R2, R1, and after R1 is closed an unqualified write lands on R2; run `/clear` and send one prompt, and confirm its writes land on the new session's turn; edit two turns concurrently and confirm exact per-turn content; attempt a write to a canceled turn and confirm `persisted:false code: skipped_terminal` with exit 1; confirm the stop gate blocks until every open turn is closed by the model.\n628: - Phase B live check (after 1.120.0, the S9 Node core release, and S10): new turn shows `agentReview.status=Unstarted`, `hostileReview.status=Unstarted`; set `requestClass: Chore` -> hostile becomes `Unnecessary`; record agent review 0.98/0.98 -> derived `Pass` with stamped thresholds; 0.9799999999999999999999999999 -> `Fail`; supplied `Pass` with 0.97 -> 422 `review_status_conflict`; `otherNotes` with `Fail` -> 400 `review_other_notes_not_allowed`; `Other` without `otherNotes` -> 400 `review_other_notes_required`; complete a `Code` turn with hostile `Unstarted` -> `session_turn_completion_gate`; record hostile review from an HV receipt (with jsonl