{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command '\"'$l=Get-Content -LiteralPath \"/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md\"; for($i=441;$i -le 550 -and $i -le $l.Count;$i++){ \"{0,3}: {1}\" -f $i,$l[$i-1] }'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"441: - TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002 (TR:2695). Changes: drop \"supersede None\" from the statement and AC003; AC002 identity immutability applies per turn. New AC: TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC004 per-turn identity binding across multiple open turns [A4].\n442: - TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002 (TEST:1142). Changes: AC001's supersession case becomes the no-cancel case; AC002's exit list adds `skipped_terminal`; \"Stop ordering\" becomes no-auto-close. New ACs: TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC005 no-cancel [A4]; -AC006 skipped_terminal exit [A5]; -AC007 stop gate blocks and never closes [A7].\n443: - FR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 (FR:2360, `ac-1`). Changes: \"Superseded hook turns persist canceled with planFile and todoId None sentinels\" becomes \"Client-supplied canceled turns persist with None sentinels\" (server path kept; no hook producer). New AC: `ac-2` hooks never produce canceled turns [A4].\n444: - TR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 (TR:3261, `ac-1`). Changes: \"Plugin superseded persist stamps planFile and todoId None and uses UpsertTurn\" becomes \"Client-supplied canceled persists stamp None\". No new AC.\n445: - TEST-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 (TEST:1355) and TEST-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-006 (TEST:1375). Changes: wording \"superseded hook persist\" becomes \"client-supplied canceled persist\"; server tests unchanged [A4 wording only].\n446: - TR-MCP-REPL-019 (TR:2427) \"Supersede preserves a server-refined turn title\". Changes: status superseded; the supersede path is deleted (TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003). Its intent (a refined title is never clobbered) moves to new AC TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003-AC005 per-turn edits never overwrite another turn's title [A4].\n447: - TR-MCP-REPL-015 (TR:2399). Changes: remove \"supersede\" from the incidental re-submit list; add the decision-list verbs and recordReview to it. New ACs: TR-MCP-REPL-015-AC001 title omitted on incidental re-submit of decision-list verbs [A6]; -AC002 recordReview never sends a title [S8].\n448: - FR-MCP-REPL-010 (FR:1951). Changes: inline AC (1) \"the active turn\" becomes \"the turn resolved by the explicit requestId override or the invocation's host-context binding (D2)\"; inline AC (3) drops \"supersede\". New structured ACs: FR-MCP-REPL-010-AC001 setTurnTitle targets an explicit requestId [A4]; -AC002 re-submits never revert titles [A4].\n449: - TEST-MCP-REPL-030 (TEST:1046) and TEST-MCP-REPL-040 (TEST:1066). Changes: remove the supersede cases; add the per-turn targeted title case. New ACs: TEST-MCP-REPL-030-AC001, TEST-MCP-REPL-040-AC001 [A4].\n450: \n451: Persist outcomes and per-turn edits\n452: - FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003 (FR:2092) \"Three session-log persist outcomes\". Changes: title becomes \"Session-log persist outcomes\"; AC001 enumerates four outcomes (primary persisted, degraded queued, failed/lost, and per-turn skipped_terminal); AC002 adds per-turn `turns[]` outcome fields; AC003 \"honored only when it matches the active turn\" becomes \"honored when it identifies the current or a registered open turn\"; statement \"appendActions refuses a request-id mismatch\" becomes \"refuses an unknown requestId\". New ACs: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC008 skipped_terminal is reported as not persisted with non-zero exit [A1 server, A5 plugin]; -AC009 explicit requestId targets an open turn [A4].\n453: - TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003 (TR:2706) \"Wrapper three-outcome exit contract\". Changes: title \"Wrapper outcome exit contract\"; AC001/AC002 add skipped_terminal and forbid persisted:true for a skipped turn; \"appendActions honors requestId\" becomes explicit target resolution. New AC: TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC005 per-turn outcome mapping from server `turns[]` [A5].\n454: - FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001 (FR:1622). Changes: unchecked AC at FR:1633 adds `skipped_terminal` to the outcomes every entrypoint normalizes; AC at FR:1632 workflow list adds one-turn-per-prompt, explicit-requestId edits, recordReview, requestClass, and the completion gate. New ACs: `ac-8` every plugin entrypoint maps skipped_terminal identically [A9]; `ac-9` every entrypoint records requestClass and both reviews and honors the gate [S8, S9].\n455: \n456: Stop gate\n457: - FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005 (FR:2118). Changes: AC001 drops \"auto-close\"; statement \"the active turn\" becomes \"every open request turn\". New ACs: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC006 the stop gate never closes a turn [A7]; -AC007 it blocks while any request turn opened since the last stop is in_progress [A7].\n458: - TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005 (TR:2730). Changes: `Close-PluginTurnIfNeeded` blocks instead of closing; \"exact-turn proof\" applies to every open turn. New AC: TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC005 findings function is pure and IO is separated [A7].\n459: \n460: Server turn model, sections, gate, sanitization\n461: - FR-SUPPORT-013 (FR:2641, `ac-4`) \"Terminal-turn audit-evidence gate enforced only for QBAgent\". Changes: the QBAgent evidence gate stays QBAgent-only; the statement adds that the requestClass and review completion gate (FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002) applies to all agents. New AC: `ac-5` the completion gate applies to standard agents [S10].\n462: - TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003 (TR:2756) \"Terminal-turn compliance gate is QBAgent-only\". Changes: \"standard agents SHALL be able to complete or fail a turn with no decision/action/commit items\" stays true for the evidence gate but is qualified by the completion gate; inline AC2 (tool descriptions) must describe both gates. New ACs: TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003-AC001 evidence gate QBAgent-only (former AC1) [S10]; -AC002 complete/fail tool descriptions state both gates [S5].\n463: - TEST-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003 (TEST:1174). New AC: TEST-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003-AC001 ClaudeCode completion with class and terminal reviews but no evidence items is accepted; without class it is rejected by the completion gate [S10].\n464: - FR-SUPPORT-014 (FR:2651), TR-SUPPORT-CORE-014 (TR:3809), TEST-SUPPORT-014 (TEST:1532). Changes: complete/fail lifecycle operations run the completion gate; the review write path goes through UpsertTurnAsync (TR ac-4 single point of truth). New ACs: FR `ac-4` complete/fail enforce the completion gate [S10]; TR `ac-5` record review uses UpsertTurnAsync [S4]; TEST `ac-5` complete without class returns 400 [S10].\n465: - FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGSAN-001 (FR:2142, `ac-1`). Changes: the redacted field list adds requestClass and both review records (otherNotes, reasons, reviewer, requestJsonlPath, responseJsonlPath). New AC: `ac-6` review text fields are redacted on every read surface [S4].\n466: - TR-MCP-DTO-001 (TR:924) \"Extended Session Log Entry Fields\". Changes: the turn DTO field list adds requestClass, agentReview, hostileReview; marker prompt session-logging instructions require classification, self-review, and turn closure. New ACs: TR-MCP-DTO-001-AC001 DTO fields present on server and client [S2]; -AC002 marker prompt instructions updated [S11].\n467: - FR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (FR:1268), TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (TR:661), TEST-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (TEST:612). Changes: \"finalizing the open turn\" becomes \"finalizing every open request turn\", and completeTurn there satisfies the completion gate. New ACs: TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001 clear-session closes every open turn [S8]; TEST-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001 skill text lists the gate steps [S11].\n468: \n469: Related, unchanged (no edits; listed so reviewers can check): FR/TR/TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 (replay of a `skipped_terminal` record must delete the failsafe, covered by A5 tests); FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGCTX-001 and TR/TEST-MCP-SESSIONLOG-006 (planFile/todoId; pattern reused); FR-SUPPORT-015 / TR-SUPPORT-CORE-015 (additive merge; reviews replace whole records, documented as a single-valued section, not a collection); FR-SUPPORT-012, TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-001/002/005; TR-MCP-SESSIONLOGSAN-001/002; FR-MCP-TRIAGEPLUGIN-001 (strengthened, no edit); FR-MCP-REPL-009, TR-MCP-REPL-010; TR-MCP-PLUGININT-001, TEST-MCP-PLUGININT-001 (generic outcome catalog gains skipped_terminal through FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001); TR-MCP-CLIENT-001 (new client body types registered); TR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-002 (`Mcp:SessionLog` options section that hosts ReviewThresholds); FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-001..006 (separate subsystem; the turn `hostileReview` record is distinct and links by requestId); FR-MCP-143 (historical text); FR-MCP-USECASE-003/006/010 (coverage); TR-MCP-DB-006 (review section delete runs under the per-session lock). Pre-existing drift noted, not fixed here: FR-SUPPORT-013 `ac-3` and TEST-SUPPORT-010C-3 / TEST-SUPPORT-022 still describe PUT as 405 (triage).\n470: \n471: ### Use cases (new, 9)\n472: \n473: UC-1 Log each user request as exactly one turn. Actors: Operator, agent host (any of the nine), plugin hooks or tools, model. Precondition: workspace trusted (marker signature and health nonce verified). Basic flow: operator submits a prompt; host delivers it to its arrival mechanism (the prompt hook, or the host-native adapter, D6); plugin classifies it as a user request, takes the turn-open lock, derives the nonce from the event (host binding table), and asks the server to mint the requestId (the server opens the turn); plugin records the token as the host session's write target (the prompt is delivered to the model at once) and in the stop ledger; every verb the model invokes is bound automatically to the host session's write target at invocation start; model closes the turn. Alternate flows: the mint call is retried or replayed and returns the same requestId; a doubly registered hook delivers the event twice and both deliveries get the same requestId; the server is unreachable and a provisional `pending-<nonce>` turn is rebound on drain; an identical prompt sent again later is a new event and opens a second turn; background event is skipped; operator sends a message mid-turn, the arrival bridge mints its turn at enqueue without touching the running turn or the write target, the message is delivered (absorbed into the running turn, or dequeued and claimed by the prompt hook) and from then on writes bind to it unless the model passes the earlier requestId; the operator pulls a queued message back (`popAll`) before delivery, the request is withdrawn, and the stop gate asks the model to fail it; a verb without a host session key in a workspace with two live sessions is refused rather than guessed; a subagent's hooks fire and leave this session's turns unchanged; while two delivered requests are open an unqualified verb is refused with `request_ambiguous` and the model names the requestId (D9); on Copilot with more than one MCP prompt hook registered the hook reports `turn_logging_unsupported` and mints nothing (D11); on a host with no arrival mechanism every session-log verb reports `turn_logging_unsupported` (D6). Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001, -002, -003, -007, -008; updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001, FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002, FR-MCP-REPL-010, FR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001.\n474: \n475: UC-2 Persist session-log writes with truthful receipts. Actors: model, plugin, server. Basic flow: model calls a verb; plugin persists; server returns per-turn outcome; plugin reports persisted only for created/merged. Alternate: target turn is terminal, server reports `skipped_terminal`, plugin reports `persisted:false`, exits non-zero, clears the failsafe; legacy server without outcomes yields `outcomeVerified:false`. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004; updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003, FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001.\n476: \n477: UC-3 Close every request turn before stopping. Actors: model, host Stop hook. Basic flow: model records actions/decisions (incl. via `designDecisions`) and closes each turn; Stop hook finds all closed with evidence and passes, clearing the ledger. Alternate: a turn is open or lacks evidence or fails the completion gate, the Stop hook blocks with the reason and never closes turns itself. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005, -006; updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005, FR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001.\n478: \n479: UC-4 Classify a request. Actors: model. Basic flow: model sets `requestClass` (Code, Docs, Chore) on its turn; hostile record flips to Unnecessary for Chore. Alternate: invalid value rejected. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001, FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006.\n480: \n481: UC-5 Complete or fail a turn under the completion gate. Actors: model, server, server-internal writers. Basic flow: model completes; gate checks class and review statuses; turn completes. Alternate: gate unmet, 400 with missing items, turn stays in progress; fail requires only class; exempt origins bypass. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002, -003, -004; updated FR-SUPPORT-013, FR-SUPPORT-014.\n482: \n483: UC-6 Record an agent self-review. Actors: model via any of the nine plugins. Basic flow: model records `agentReview` (Running, then scores); server derives Pass/Fail from thresholds and stamps them. Alternate: conflicting supplied status 422; invalid fields 400; review recorded after completion. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001, -002, -003, -006, -008, FR-SUPPORT-016 (new); updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGSAN-001.\n484: \n485: UC-7 Record a hostile validation review with receipts. Actors: hostile reviewer (Codex CLI, gpt-6-sol, xhigh), coordinator agent. Basic flow: at the end of each slice once its gates are green, and at P0's end (D10), the coordinator writes the HV brief and launches the Codex reviewer; the runner records the request and response jsonl; the reviewer writes its markdown and JSON receipts; the coordinator records `hostileReview` from the receipt (accuracy/completeness mapped, receipt paths set). Alternate: DISAGREE with passing scores recorded as Other with notes; missing receipt paths rejected; a run whose live model or effort is not gpt-6-sol/xhigh is not accepted as HV; Code or Docs turns of the slice that completed before its HV carry `Other` \"pending slice HV <gate>\" and receive the slice verdict through `recordReview`. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002, -005.\n486: \n487: UC-8 Configure review pass thresholds. Actors: operator. Basic flow: operator sets thresholds per kind and score (or per instance); startup and ValidateConfig accept them; new reviews derive with them and stamp them. Alternate: value outside [0,1] rejected. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-007.\n488: \n489: UC-9 Read review scores losslessly. Actors: agents, client apps. Basic flow: a client reads a turn through REST, MCP, client, REPL, or a plugin and gets the exact decimal scores. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004.\n490: \n491: ## TDD AC allocation by phase\n492: \n493: Two kinds of AC. Baseline-green ACs document behavior that exists and passes today; this plan has exactly five (FR-SUPPORT-016 `ac-1`..`ac-4` and TR-SUPPORT-CORE-016 `ac-1`); they need a green receipt from the existing named tests run in P0 (`dotnet test tests/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Tests -c Debug --filter \"FullyQualifiedName~SessionLogServiceReplaceDeleteTests\"`, zero failures, zero skips), no RED, and must stay green at every later gate. Every other AC is new or changed behavior and is assigned to the slice that writes its RED test first; extension slices add the same AC on their surface. Per slice, all listed new or changed ACs must be RED before code, mocks-green before production code, and green at the slice gate; the phase HV verifies every new or changed AC of the phase has its RED and green receipts and every baseline-green AC its green receipts.\n494: \n495: - P0 (no product tests): creates every requirement, AC, mapping, and use case; AC allocation itself is a P0 HV claim.\n496: - Phase A\n497:   - A1: SESSIONTURN-004-001, -003; SESSIONTURN-001-001..003 (server mint).\n498:   - A2: SESSIONTURN-001-006, -007.\n499:   - A3: SESSIONTURN-001-001..004, -008, -009, -010 (plugin); SESSIONTURN-002-001, -002.\n500:   - A4: SESSIONTURN-001-005; SESSIONTURN-002-003; SESSIONTURN-003-001, -002, -004; SESSIONTURN-007-001..008.\n501:   - A5: SESSIONTURN-004-002, -004, -005; extension of SESSIONTURN-001-008 (drain rebinding through the persist path).\n502:   - A6: SESSIONTURN-006-001..003.\n503:   - A7: SESSIONTURN-003-003; SESSIONTURN-005-001, -002, -004..009.\n504:   - A8: SESSIONTURN-008-001, -002, -004; Node-core extensions of SESSIONTURN-001-001..004, -008, -002-001..003, -003-001, -002, -004-002, -004, -006-001, -007-001..008.\n505:   - A9: SESSIONTURN-008-003, -005, -006; extension of -008-004.\n506: - Phase B\n507:   - S1: SESSIONCLASS-001-001, -002; SESSIONCLASS-002-001, -002, -006 (policy and message); SESSIONREVIEW-003-001..006; SESSIONREVIEW-004-002, -003; SESSIONREVIEW-006-001..005; SESSIONREVIEW-007-002..004; SESSIONREVIEW-008-004.\n508:   - S2: SESSIONREVIEW-001-001; SESSIONREVIEW-004-001 (client JSON hop); extension of -004-002.\n509:   - S3: SESSIONCLASS-001-004; SESSIONREVIEW-001-006; SESSIONREVIEW-004-001 (storage hops).\n510:   - S4: SESSIONCLASS-001-003, -005; SESSIONREVIEW-001-002..005; SESSIONREVIEW-002-001, -004; SESSIONREVIEW-003-007; SESSIONREVIEW-006-002, -003 (service); SESSIONREVIEW-007-001, -005, -006; extension of -007-003.\n511:   - S5: SESSIONCLASS-001-006 (REST/MCP/client); extensions of SESSIONCLASS-001-002, -002-006 (classifier), SESSIONREVIEW-001-005, -002-001, -002, -004, -003-007, -004-001 (REST/MCP), -004-003, -006-004, -007-003.\n512:   - S6: SESSIONREVIEW-004-001 (REPL hops); extensions of SESSIONCLASS-001-006, SESSIONREVIEW-002-002, -003, -003-007.\n513:   - S7: SESSIONCLASS-001-006 (McpAgent); TR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004 ACs.\n514:   - S8: SESSIONTURN-005-003; SESSIONCLASS-004-001..003; SESSIONREVIEW-002-002, -003 (PowerShell); SESSIONREVIEW-004-001 (PowerShell hops); SESSIONREVIEW-005-001..003; SESSIONREVIEW-008-003.\n515:   - S9: SESSIONREVIEW-008-001, -002; Node-core extensions of SESSIONTURN-005-003, SESSIONCLASS-004-001..003, SESSIONREVIEW-002-002, -003, -004-001, -005-001..003.\n516:   - S10: SESSIONCLASS-002-001..005 (server enforcement); SESSIONCLASS-003-001..004.\n517:   - S11: documentation contract tests for every FR; SESSIONREVIEW-008-005 (feature matrix review rows); full-suite re-verification of all ACs.\n518: - Every TR AC is allocated to the slice in brackets on that TR above.\n519: - Updated-requirement ACs by slice (also bracketed in \"Updated existing requirements\"):\n520:   - A1: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC008 (server).\n521:   - A3: TR-MCP-PLUGIN-013-AC001, -AC002, -AC004; TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-013-AC001; TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC001; FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001-AC007.\n522:   - A4: TR-MCP-PLUGIN-013-AC003; TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-013-AC002; FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001-AC006; FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC006; TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC004; TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC005; FR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 ac-2; TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003-AC005 (from retired TR-MCP-REPL-019); FR-MCP-REPL-010-AC001, -AC002; TEST-MCP-REPL-030-AC001; TEST-MCP-REPL-040-AC001; FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC009.\n523:   - A5: TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC006; FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC008 (plugin); TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC005.\n524:   - A6: TR-MCP-REPL-015-AC001.\n525:   - A7: TR-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC001..AC003; TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC002; TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC007; FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC006, -AC007; TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005-AC005.\n526:   - A9: FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001 ac-8.\n527:   - S2: TR-MCP-DTO-001-AC001.\n528:   - S4: rename every legacy `FR-SUPPORT-010G` citation in source and tests to FR-SUPPORT-016 (36 citations, 9 files; comment and test-name text only, verified by `rg -n -F FR-SUPPORT-010G src tests` returning nothing); FR-SUPPORT-016 ac-5 (service); TR-SUPPORT-CORE-016 ac-2, ac-3 (service); TR-SUPPORT-CORE-014 ac-5; FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGSAN-001 ac-6.\n529:   - S5: FR-SUPPORT-016 ac-5 (REST/MCP/client); TR-SUPPORT-CORE-016 ac-3 (surfaces); TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003-AC002.\n530:   - S8: TR-MCP-REPL-015-AC002; FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001 ac-9 (PowerShell hosts); TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001.\n531:   - S9: FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001 ac-9 (TypeScript hosts).\n532:   - S10: FR-SUPPORT-013 ac-5; TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003-AC001; TEST-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003-AC001; FR-SUPPORT-014 ac-4; TEST-SUPPORT-014 ac-5.\n533:   - S11: TR-MCP-DTO-001-AC002; TEST-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001.\n534:   - P0 (no new tests): the five baseline-green ACs (FR-SUPPORT-016 ac-1..ac-4, TR-SUPPORT-CORE-016 ac-1) are created for existing behavior and verified green by the existing `SessionLogServiceReplaceDeleteTests` run in P0.\n535: - Phase HV claims include: every new or changed AC above has a RED receipt (TRX or Pester/jest result with the failing assertion) recorded on its slice TODO before code, and a green receipt at the slice gate; every baseline-green AC has its P0 green receipt and stays green at each phase gate; any AC without its required receipts is a FAIL.\n536: \n537: ## Wire contracts (documented in P0 before tests)\n538: \n539: Phase A\n540: - `SessionLogSubmitResult` 201 body adds `turns: [{ requestId, outcome, storedStatus, reason }]`, `outcome` in `created|merged|skipped_terminal|skipped_duplicate`. MCP `sessionlog_submit` returns `{ success, id, turns }`. Status code stays 201 (late-hook snapshot protection).\n541: - Plugin receipt on `skipped_terminal`: `code: skipped_terminal`, `persisted: false`, `storedStatus`, `reason`; verb returns false; exit 1; failsafe cleared.\n542: - Hook statuses: new `system-event-skipped`, `turn-open-contended`; `turn-already-open` when a mint returns `merged` (same nonce).\n543: - Stop gate: blocks `turn_in_progress` (any ledger or registered turn still in_progress), `turn_missing_model_evidence` (closed with zero model-authored actions and decisions), `session_turn_completion_gate` (after S8), failed build after edits (existing), stale session (existing); blocks `turn_withdrawn_unclosed` (a withdrawn queued request still in_progress); warns on canceled/queued/degraded, on `duplicate_delivery_suspected`, `ingress_nonce_source_missing`, `arrival_bridge_format_unrecognized`; re-evaluates on every Stop, including `stop_hook_active=true`, blocking again while turns are open and recording `stop_gate_overridden_by_host` if the host stops anyway; passes with `{}` and clears closed entries. Auto-close removed. Block text: `session_turn_stop_gate: <n> turn(s) are not closed correctly: <id> (<code>: <detail>); ... Close each turn yourself with workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn or workflow.sessionlog.failTurn (pass requestId for earlier open turns) after recording at least one action or designDecision; the stop gate never closes turns for you.`\n544: - Ingress mint (D1): `POST /qbrainai/sessionlog/{agent}/{sessionId}/mint` (also `/mcpserver/sessionlog/...`), client `MintTurnAsync` and REPL `workflow.sessionlog.mintTurn` (hook and adapter callers only; no MCP tool), exactly as TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004 AC-005 specifies: first mint 201 `outcome: created`; same nonce in the same session 200 `outcome: merged` with the same requestId. Failsafe mint record: `{ method: workflow.sessionlog.mintTurn, params: { ingressNonce, queryTitle, queryText, model, planFile: None, todoId: None }, provisionalRequestId: pending-<nonce>, hostSessionKey }` (hooks send the `None` sentinels; a later update sets the real values).\n545: - Arrival bridge (D5): `sessions/<key>/arrival-bridge.pid` and the `turn-state.yaml` lifecycle below (no separate offset file); hook statuses add `turn-claimed-from-bridge`.\n546: - Plugin per-turn store: `turns/<requestId>.yaml` (one file per turn, own lock `turns/<requestId>.lock`), `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/turn-state.yaml` `{ writeTarget: { requestId, deliveredAtUtc, source: prompt-hook | absorbed-mid-turn } | null, openDelivered: [requestId], queue: [{ requestId, nonce, enqueueOffset, enqueueTimestamp, promptSha256, state: queued | delivered | withdrawn, stateOffset }], appliedThroughOffset }` (written only by the arrival bridge, the prompt hook, and the close verbs, each write one atomic replace under `turn-open.lock`), `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/ended.yaml`, `current-turn.yaml` kept only as a read-only legacy status file `{ turnRequestId }` never used for targeting, `stop-ledger.yaml` (per host session), all under `turn-open.lock`. No prompt ledger and no dedupe window. Every verb invocation carries a binding `{ hostSessionKey, requestId, boundAtUtc }` captured once at start (D2) and stored in its persist and failsafe records; failsafe paths and fingerprints include the bound requestId. Verbs accept an explicit `requestId` override, required while two or more delivered requests are open (`request_ambiguous`, D9); unknown ids are refused with `request_unknown`.\n547: \n548: Phase B turn shape (additive on `UnifiedRequestEntryDto`, server and client)\n549: ```json\n550: \"requestClass\": \"Code\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/pwsh -Command \"pwsh.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command '\"'$l=Get-Content -LiteralPath \"/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md\"; for($i=221;$i -le 330 -and $i -le $l.Count;$i++){ \"{0,3}: {1}\" -f $i,$l[$i-1] }'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"221: FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005 The stop gate enforces and never closes turns.\n222: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC001 Blocks with `turn_in_progress` when any request turn opened since the last stop is still in progress. [A7]\n223: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC002 Blocks with `turn_missing_model_evidence` when a closed turn has no model-authored action or design decision. [A7]\n224: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC003 Blocks with `session_turn_completion_gate` when the completion gate is unmet. [S8 +S9]\n225: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC004 Never calls `completeTurn` or `failTurn`. [A7]\n226: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC005 Warns without blocking for model-canceled turns, retained failsafe records, and degraded persistence. [A7]\n227: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC006 Passes and clears the ledger only when every check passes. Every Stop invocation re-evaluates the ledger, including when the host reports that an earlier Stop already blocked (Claude Code `stop_hook_active`, Grok `stopHookActive`): while any turn remains open it blocks again with the same findings. If the host ends the session anyway (its own continuation limit), the gate records `stop_gate_overridden_by_host` with the open turn ids in the ledger, and the next SessionStart or prompt hook shows it as a warning until the model closes those turns. [A7]\n228: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC007 The existing failed-build block is retained. [A7]\n229: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC008 Warns (never merges, never blocks) with `duplicate_delivery_suspected` when one host session minted two requestIds within 2 seconds for prompts whose SHA-256 of the normalized text is equal, naming both requestIds so the operator can check hook registration; the warning is diagnostic only (it can fire only where a host's event identity is weaker than expected) and is not evidence of D1 compliance. [A7]\n230: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC009 Blocks with `turn_withdrawn_unclosed` while a `withdrawn` request is still `in_progress`, naming it, its withdrawal record (`popAll` or `remove` reason), and the action: close it with `workflow.sessionlog.failTurn` (`requestId` override, reason \"withdrawn before delivery\"); hooks still never close it. [A7]\n231: \n232: FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-006 Decision lists through workflow verbs.\n233: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-006-AC001 `updateTurn`, `appendActions`, `completeTurn`, `failTurn` accept `designDecisions`, `requirementsDiscovered`, `blockers` and persist them. [A6 +A8]\n234: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-006-AC002 Those lists are part of the dedupe fingerprint, so a change to only them is persisted. [A6]\n235: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-006-AC003 Model-evidence counters count only model-invoked verbs, never hook-invoked ones. [A6]\n236: \n237: FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007 Independent turn edits.\n238: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC001 Each turn has its own state file and lock; each host session has one state file `sessions/<hostSessionKey>/turn-state.yaml` holding its write target (the request most recently delivered to the model; D9 refuses unqualified writes while several delivered requests are open), its open delivered requests, its queue (minted requests with `queued`/`delivered`/`withdrawn` state), and `appliedThroughOffset`, always replaced atomically (temp file, flush, rename) under `turn-open.lock`; `current-turn.yaml` remains only as a read-only legacy status file that no verb uses for targeting. [A4 +A8]\n239: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC002 Every verb resolves exactly one target turn, in this precedence: explicit `requestId` override, else the invocation's bound request, which is refused with `request_ambiguous` while two or more delivered requests are open in the host session (D9); it mutates only that turn; an unknown explicit requestId is refused with `request_unknown`, and a terminal one with `turn_immutable` (except the review and class writes allowed on terminal turns, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004-AC004). [A4 +A8]\n240: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC003 Concurrent edits to two turns from separate processes lose nothing and cross-contaminate nothing. [A4 +A8]\n241: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC004 Failsafe records and fingerprints are namespaced by requestId; replay never targets another turn. [A4 +A8]\n242: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC005 Opening, closing, or canceling one turn never changes another turn locally or on the server. [A4 +A8]\n243: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC006 Host-context binding (operator D2): at the start of each verb invocation the plugin resolves the invoking host session's key by the host's locked method (see the host binding table) and binds the invocation to that host session's write target; the binding is written into the invocation's persist and failsafe records and never re-resolved, so a prompt minted after the invocation started never retargets it. [A4 +A8]\n244: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC007 Interleaving: with R1 delivered and R2 enqueued mid-turn in the same host session, a verb started after R2's mint but before R2's delivery (`absorbed_mid_turn` or `dequeue`) writes to R1; a verb started after R2's delivery without `requestId` is refused with `request_ambiguous` while R1 and R2 are both open (D9); with explicit ids an R1, R2, R1 sequence of writes lands on R1, R2, R1 respectively; once R1 is closed an unqualified verb writes to R2; a withdrawn R2 never becomes a write target; R1 stays in progress throughout. When the verb cannot read its host session key, the live-session rule applies: with exactly one live host session of its agent it binds there with warning `host_session_inferred`; with none or several it is refused (`host_session_unknown`, `host_session_ambiguous`) unless it carries an explicit `requestId`; with two concurrent host sessions in one workspace and no keys, zero writes land on the wrong turn. [A4 +A8]\n245: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007-AC008 Session changes in place never misattribute: after Claude Code `/clear`, a shell verb binds to the new session's write target (its `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` is updated), a long-lived process resolves per call by the live-session rule (the cleared session is ended by SessionEnd reason `clear`), and after resume the resumed session's key is used. [A4 +A8]\n246: \n247: FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008 All agent plugins enforce the turn rules.\n248: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008-AC001 The Node core satisfies the SESSIONTURN-001..007 behaviors for its tools and cache (jest). [A8]\n249: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008-AC002 cline, cline-v2, and opencode adopt the Node core and pass their suites. [A8]\n250: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008-AC003 claude-code, claude-cowork, codex, copilot, grok, and grok-bot receive the synced PowerShell core and pass their suites. [A9]\n251: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008-AC004 Every host either has an arrival mechanism listed in the host binding table (operator D6) or reports `turn_logging_unsupported` on every session-log verb and writes nothing; no host relies on the model to open turns. [A8 +A9]\n252: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008-AC005 All nine plugin versions are bumped and reported correctly by the marker `agent_plugins` section after a server restart. [A9]\n253: - FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008-AC006 `docs/AGENT-PLUGIN-FEATURE-MATRIX.md` lists, for each of the nine plugins and each turn-logging feature (ingress mint, arrival bridge or adapter, host-context binding, stop gate), whether it is supported, adapted, or a documented capability limitation (D7) with the reason and the P0.2 receipt; every `turn_logging_unsupported` host appears there as a limitation. [A9]\n254: \n255: FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001 Request classification.\n256: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001-AC001 `requestClass` accepts `Code`, `Docs`, `Chore` case-insensitively and returns PascalCase. [S1]\n257: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001-AC002 Other values, empty strings, and `Unclassified` from agent surfaces are rejected with `request_class_invalid`. [S1 +S5]\n258: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001-AC003 An omitted value keeps the stored value on additive writes; PUT replace resets it. [S4]\n259: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001-AC004 The migration backfills existing rows with `Unclassified`. [S3]\n260: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001-AC005 Turns can be created and updated without a class. [S4]\n261: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001-AC006 The field is readable and writable on REST, MCP, client, REPL, and McpAgent. [S5 +S6 +S7]\n262: \n263: FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002 Completion gate.\n264: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002-AC001 `completed` requires `requestClass`, `agentReview` in Pass/Fail/Other, and for Code/Docs `hostileReview` in Pass/Fail/Other; for Chore `hostileReview` is not checked. [S1 policy, S10 enforcement]\n265: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002-AC002 `failed` requires `requestClass` only. [S1, S10]\n266: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002-AC003 The gate applies on every surface: submit, upsert, PATCH, PUT, complete, fail, MCP tools, REPL, McpAgent. [S10]\n267: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002-AC004 It fires only on a transition into `completed`/`failed` or a PUT carrying a terminal status; additive writes to already-terminal turns are not re-gated. [S10]\n268: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002-AC005 A rejection is atomic and leaves the data context reusable. [S10]\n269: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002-AC006 The error is 400 `validation_error` with token `session_turn_completion_gate` and missing items in fixed order (requestClass, agentReview, hostileReview). [S1 message, S5 classifier, S10]\n270: \n271: FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-003 Exempt write origins.\n272: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-003-AC001 Import, ServerInternal, and Replication origins bypass the gate. [S10]\n273: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-003-AC002 ServerInternal writers stamp `Chore`; Import and Replication stamp `Unclassified` when no class arrives; no review is ever fabricated. [S10]\n274: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-003-AC003 No REST, MCP, REPL, client, or plugin code can select a non-Agent origin (architecture test). [S10]\n275: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-003-AC004 QBAgent internal tool completions are gated. [S10]\n276: \n277: FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004 Plugin class and gate surfaces.\n278: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004-AC001 Plugin verbs accept `requestClass`. [S8 +S9]\n279: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004-AC002 A local pre-check fails closed with the exact gate message before any persist. [S8 +S9]\n280: - FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004-AC003 A server gate rejection clears the failsafe and leaves the turn in progress. [S8 +S9]\n281: \n282: FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001 Turn review records.\n283: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001-AC001 Each turn exposes `agentReview` and `hostileReview` with fields `status`, `otherNotes`, `correctness`, `completeness`, `correctnessThreshold`, `completenessThreshold`, `reasons`, `reviewer`, `reviewedAt`, `requestJsonlPath`, `responseJsonlPath`. [S2]\n284: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001-AC002 The server creates `agentReview=Unstarted` and `hostileReview=Unstarted` at turn creation. [S4]\n285: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001-AC003 A review write replaces the whole record (latest wins, reasons not merged); an identical write is a no-op. [S4]\n286: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001-AC004 An omitted review keeps the stored record; a PUT turn omitting it and a section DELETE reset it to the default status. [S4]\n287: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001-AC005 Every read surface returns both records, sanitized (REST, MCP, client, REPL, federation snapshot, transaction restore). [S4 +S5]\n288: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001-AC006 Existing rows are backfilled with `agentReview=Unstarted` and `hostileReview=Unstarted`. [S3]\n289: \n290: FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002 Review writes on any turn status.\n291: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC001 Section PUT `agentReview`/`hostileReview` works on in-progress, completed, failed, canceled, and legacy turns and changes no other field or status. [S4 +S5]\n292: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC002 `recordReview` (MCP tool, client, REPL, plugins) writes only the review. [S5 +S6 +S8 +S9]\n293: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC003 Other mutations of terminal turns stay refused by the REPL and plugins. [S6 +S8 +S9]\n294: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC004 Item DELETE on a review section returns 400. [S4 +S5]\n295: \n296: FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003 Per-status field validation.\n297: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC001 `Unnecessary`/`Unstarted` carry no data fields. [S1]\n298: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC002 `Running` requires `reviewer` and forbids scores. [S1]\n299: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC003 `Pass`/`Fail` require `correctness`, `completeness`, `reviewer`, `reviewedAt`; `hostileReview` `Pass`/`Fail` also require both jsonl paths. [S1]\n300: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC004 `Other` requires `otherNotes` with at least one non-whitespace character (rejected otherwise with `review_other_notes_required`); scores, `reasons`, `reviewer`, `reviewedAt`, and receipt paths are optional. [S1]\n301: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC005 `otherNotes` with text is rejected unless status is `Other`. [S1]\n302: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC006 Scores lie in [0,1]; `reviewer` <= 256 chars; paths <= 2048 chars; `reviewedAt` needs an explicit offset and is stored UTC; reason items are non-empty. [S1]\n303: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC007 Validation runs before any mutation on every surface. [S4 +S5 +S6]\n304: \n305: FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004 Lossless decimal scores.\n306: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004-AC001 `0.1234567890123456789` and `0.1234567890123456789012345678` round-trip unchanged through every hop: client JSON [S2], SQLite/PostgreSQL/SQL Server storage [S3], REST and MCP [S5], REPL YAML quoted/unquoted and JsonElement [S6], PowerShell plugin YAML block/flow and JSON [S8], Node core and TypeScript hosts [S9].\n307: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004-AC002 A JSON number or numeric string is accepted when its raw text matches `^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$` (no sign, no exponent) with a value in [0,1]; a normalized number (trailing fractional zeros stripped) is returned. [S1 +S2]\n308: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004-AC003 Validation runs on the raw lexeme before any numeric conversion, so nothing is ever rounded: more than 28 fractional digits is rejected with `review_score_precision` (e.g. `0.12345678901234567890123456789`, which `JsonElement.TryGetDecimal` would round), exponent or signed forms with `review_score_format`, and values outside [0,1] with `review_score_out_of_range`; each case is tested as a JSON number, a JSON string, an unquoted YAML scalar, and a quoted YAML scalar. [S1 +S5 +S6 +S8 +S9]\n309: \n310: FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-005 Hostile validation receipt mapping.\n311: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-005-AC001 `accuracy/100` maps to `correctness` and `completeness/100` to `completeness` exactly. [S8 +S9]\n312: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-005-AC002 AGREE omits status so the server derives it; DISAGREE maps to `Fail` when the scores derive Fail, and to `Other` with `otherNotes` naming the failed claims when the scores derive Pass. [S8 +S9]\n313: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-005-AC003 `reasons`, `reviewedAt`, `reviewer` come from the receipt; the Codex HV receipt (the reviewer's JSON receipt and the `--json` response jsonl) is accepted as input. [S8 +S9]\n314: \n315: FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006 Review status lifecycle.\n316: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006-AC001 Status accepts the six values case-insensitively and returns PascalCase. [S1]\n317: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006-AC002 `hostileReview` flips `Unstarted` -> `Unnecessary` when the class becomes Chore, and back when the class changes away while still `Unnecessary`. [S1 rule, S4 service]\n318: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006-AC003 Records past `Unstarted`/`Unnecessary` are never changed automatically. [S1, S4]\n319: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006-AC004 Clients cannot write `Unnecessary` or `Unstarted`. [S1 +S5]\n320: - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006-AC005