nt): no state change by itself; the prompt hook that fires for that prompt, under `turn-open.lock`, claims the oldest `queued` entry whose `promptSha256` equals its prompt's hash, sets it `delivered`, and makes it the write target (it mints with `prompt_id` only when no entry matches). `remove` with reason `absorbed_mid_turn`: the oldest `queued` entry with that `content` hash becomes `delivered` and the write target. `remove` with any other or no reason, and `popAll` (each content line it carries): the matching `queued` entry becomes `withdrawn`. Any other operation or an unrecognized shape: warning `arrival_bridge_format_unrecognized`, no state change. Each record's state change and the advance of `appliedThroughOffset` past it are one atomic replace of `turn-state.yaml` (temp file, flush, rename, under `turn-open.lock`), and records that start below `appliedThroughOffset` are skipped, so a restart never re-applies `enqueue`, `remove`, or `popAll`; the server mint for `enqueue` happens before that replace and is idempotent (same nonce, `merged`). A `remove` or `popAll` targets the oldest `queued` entry whose `promptSha256` matches and whose `enqueueOffset` is below the record's offset.\n 83: - claude-cowork: same fields and arrival bridge as claude-code. P0.2 verifies that Cowork executes plugin hooks; if it does not, Cowork has no arrival mechanism and is unsupported for turn logging under D6 (`turn_logging_unsupported`, nothing written) until it gains one. A9 repairs the dangling `bin/mcpserver-stdio.cmd` connector.\n 84: - codex: A9 adds `hooks/hooks.json` (SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse, Stop, SessionEnd per the Codex hooks reference) and keeps the manual enforcement steps in `skills/enforcement/SKILL.md` until the hook trust check below passes; nonce payload `turn_id`; hook key payload `session_id` (subagents share the parent's); verb key env `CODEX_THREAD_ID` only if P0.2 proves it equals `session_id` in shell commands, else the live-session rul