ion key `taskId`; the MCP server's tools carry no `taskId`, so they use the live-session rule; single registration is enforced as for copilot. P0.2 verifies in the installed Cline build that native hooks run, where hook scripts are installed, the payload fields, and whether queued messages fire the hook at arrival; if no arrival mechanism exists, classic Cline is unsupported for turn logging under D6 (`turn_logging_unsupported`).\n 89: - cline-v2: turn opens in `beforeRun` with nonce `runId`; host session key `conversationId` (lifecycle snapshot and tool context; the plugin stops stripping `sessionId`, `conversationId`, `runId`, `toolCallId` at `plugin.ts:122-140`); prompt text from the last user entry of `snapshot.messages`; stop-equivalent `afterRun` (no per-run session close); `@cline/core` pin raised to the version shipping `@cline/shared` 0.0.92 types. P0.2 records whether a queued message starts its own run at arrival; if it does not, the arrival adapter uses the host's message-queue event if one exists; if neither exists, cline-v2 is unsupported for turn logging under D6 (`turn_logging_unsupported`).\n 90: - opencode: turn opens in `chat.message` for user messages with nonce `messageID` (fired when the message is created, which is arrival); host session key `sessionID`; plugin tools read `_context.sessionID`, and shell commands get `MCP_HOST_SESSION_KEY` from the `shell.env` hook; stop-equivalent `session.idle`; the start/end regexes and the factory signature are replaced.\n 91: \n 92: P0 per plugin: fetch origin; resolve the remote default branch with `git ls-remote --symref origin HEAD` (`main` for eight repos, `master` for opencode on 2026-10-09); compare local uncommitted work against origin lineage (`CORE-MANIFEST.yaml` coreVersion ancestry, EOL-insensitive diff); preserve any local work in a uniquely tagged stash (record SHA); fast-forward to that default branch; record version and head; re-check every row of the host binding table against the head and record any difference as a RequirementRefined decision before A1. Never discard uncommitted work without that receipt.\n 93: \n 94: Per-plugin changes:\n 95: - PowerShell hosts (claude-code, claude-cowork, codex, copilot, grok, grok-bot): receive all plugin-core changes through `./build.ps1 SyncAgentPlugins --agent-plugin-parent /home/sharpninja/github` (A9 and S8) plus host wrappers from `hooks-templates/generate-wrappers.ps1`; host-specific glue exactly as the host binding table states (nonce source, hook and verb host-session keys, subagent and system-event markers, stop field); the A9 repairs named there (codex `hooks/hooks.json`, copilot hook path, cowork connector, grok camelCase reads, the core's `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` and `stop_hook_active` reads); duplicate-registration detection where the host can double-register hooks (A2 equivalent; Grok's default run of `~/.claude/settings.json` hooks included); skill/README docs for recordReview, requestClass, automatic binding with optional requestId override.\n 96: - TypeScript hosts (cline, cline-v2, opencode): all shared behavior changes land once in `plugins/core/lib-node` (`src/tools/session.ts`, `src/tools/session-shim.ts`, `src/cache/cache-manager.ts`, `src/runtime/host-context.ts`, `src/transport/*`) in slices A8 and S9, with jest tests in `plugins/core/lib-node/tests` (`session-shim.test.ts`, `cache-manager.test.ts`, `host-context.test.ts`, `repl-bridge.test.ts`, plus new suites). Then each plugin adopts the new packed core and adds the host glue the host binding table fixes: cline-v2 (`beforeRun` mint with `runId`, `conversationId` key, `afterRun` stop-equivalent, no per-run session close, `@cline/core` pin raised), opencode (`chat.message` mint with `messageID`, `sessionID` key via `_context` and `shell.env`, `session.idle` stop-equivalent, regex and factory replaced), cline (Cline native UserPromptSubmit hook adapter with `taskId` key and derived nonce, MCP tools on the live-session rule, or `turn_logging_unsupported` per D6); each exposes `requestClass`, `session_record_review`, the `requestId` override (required under D9 while two or more delivered requests are open), truthful outcomes, decisions/requirements/blockers.\n 97: - Every plugin: version bump, `CORE-MANIFEST.yaml` or packed-core version pin (where applicable), plugin-owned docs/skills/ENFORCEMENT.md and their tests updated; marker `agent_plugins` versions verified after server restart.\n 98: \n 99: Per-plugin test gate (G6, run for every plugin touched by a slice; zero failures, zero skips):\n100: - PowerShell hosts: `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command \"Invoke-Pester -Path tests -CI\"` and `bats tests/*.bats`.\n101: - Node core: in `plugins/core/lib-node` `npm ci; npm run build; npm test` (jest), run on each of Node 18, 20, 22, and the latest release (D12 version matrix, through the version manager the host provides, for example `mise exec node@20 -- npm test`); the TypeScript hosts run their suites on their lowest declared engine and on the latest release.\n102: - TypeScript hosts (cline, cline-v2, opencode): `npm ci; npm run build; npm test` in each repo.\n103: - `./build.ps1 PluginSessionLogIntegration` for hosts it covers.\n104: - Phase exits require G6 green for all nine plugins and the Node core.\n105: \n106: ## Coordination with QB-AGENT-001 (Codex)\n107: \n108: Observed 2026-10-09T17:14Z (read-only): Codex is implementing QB-AGENT-001 in the McpServer worktree `/home/sharpninja/github/cline/.worktrees/mcpserver-qbrain`, branch `qb/p1-governance-core`, base `f56dcf70` (this plan's baseline), uncommitted, 10 modified and 8 new files, all under `plugins/core/lib-node` (`src/tools/session.ts`, `src/tools/session-shim.ts`, `src/runtime/host-context.ts`, `src/runtime/core-config.ts`, `src/transport/repl-bridge.ts`, `src/discovery/marker-resolver.ts`, `src/index.ts`; new `src/cache/audit-outbox.ts`, `src/runtime/core-runtime-error.ts`). Its relayed status: not merge-ready; P1 carries most McpServer changes; P2 adds paginated session-turn listing and detail reads; six-platform REPL packaging runs through P5. Two current designs conflict with this plan: `host-context.ts` refuses a second turn while one is open (`session_failed`, \"The current turn must finish before another starts\"), and the session tool enum adds an undocumented action type `tool_execution`.\n109: \n110: Channel (operator, 2026-10-09: \"I suggest using a single global mcp memory to act as a coms channel for coordination\"): Global MCP memory `MEMORY-PROCESS-007`, an append-only log with the protocol written in the memory itself (read, append one entry, write back, read back; KINDs NOTICE, REQUEST, ANSWER, CONTRACT, READINESS, ACK; READINESS carries commit SHA, PR, validation evidence, and the HV verdict; operator decisions are posted as REQUEST and never settled by an agent). The implementing agent reads it at session start and before every slice that touches a shared file.\n111: \n112: Clearance (operator, 2026-10-09: \"Partial clearance\"), posted as an ANSWER in `MEMORY-PROCESS-007` at 18:08:08Z: QB-AGENT-001 P1 may continue on REPL pinning and exclusive REPL ownership, isolated child credentials, workspace-bound bootstrap, typed lifecycle failures, and the audit-outbox storage internals (`src/runtime/core-config.ts`, `src/discovery/marker-resolver.ts`, `src/transport/repl-bridge.ts`, `src/runtime/core-runtime-error.ts`, the persistence half of `src/cache/audit-outbox.ts`); the turn lifecycle in `host-context.ts`, the session lifecycle in `session.ts` and `session-shim.ts`, and the audit event and receipt shape stay on HOLD until Codex ACKs C1-C5 and C9 or the operator resolves a REQUEST. That ANSWER left slice-turn hostile reviews (its item 5) open; operator D10 settled it, and a NOTICE at 19:51:42Z posted D9, D10, D11, D12 and the proposed C9 code additions. As of 2026-10-09T19:52Z Codex had posted no ACK; P0.7 re-reads the channel and records each contract's disposition.\n113: \n114: Contract-disposition gate: no slice that changes `host-context.ts`, `session.ts`, `session-shim.ts`, the audit-outbox event or receipt shape, or the shared server session-log files is integrated or merged until Codex has posted ACK for C1-C5 and C9 in `MEMORY-PROCESS-007`, or the operator has resolved a REQUEST about each one not ACKed; each of C6-C8 and C10-C12 must be ACKed or resolved the same way before the slice that depends on it starts (C6 and C7: A6 and A8; C8: S10; C10: S9; C11: S4 and S5; C12: S6). Sequencing (order-independent): P0.7 records QB-AGENT-001's state from the channel (merged to `develop` or not, SHA). A slice that touches a shared file starts from current `develop`: if QB-AGENT-001 P1 has merged, the slice builds on it; if not, the slice proceeds and QB-AGENT-001 rebases. In both orders the contracts below hold; where landed QB-AGENT-001 code contradicts one, the slice records a RequirementRefined decision, posts a CONTRACT entry, and implements the contract on top of that code without weakening any FR of this plan. Phase B's S4 and S5 start only after a READINESS entry for QB-AGENT-001 P2 or an operator ruling posted as REQUEST/ANSWER, because both change the session-turn read surfaces.\n115: \n116: Shared contracts (posted as the first CONTRACT entry in P0.7):\n117: - C1 Multiple open turns per host session: a map of open turns by requestId plus a per-host-session write target (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC005, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003, FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-007); no single current-turn slot; \"finish before another starts\" applies per turn, never per session.\n118: - C2 Server-minted turn identity: requestIds come from the mint route (D1); an event recorded before the mint returns carries the turn's `ingressNonce` and the provisional `pending-<nonce>` id, and replay rebinds every such event to the minted requestId atomically and in original order (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC008).\n119: - C3 Outcome mapping into any Node persistence path, including an audit outbox (TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-008 AC-006): `created` and `merged` -> `persisted`; `skipped_duplicate` -> `unchanged`; `skipped_terminal` -> `rejected` with reason `skipped_terminal`, never retried or quarantined, failsafe record cleared; a server without per-turn outcomes -> `outcomeVerified:false`.\n120: - C4 Every persisted or queued event carries its immutable D2 binding `{ hostSessionKey, keySource, requestId, boundAtUtc }`; replay never re-resolves it.\n121: - C5 State is scoped per host session key (host binding table), not per process; one process may serve several host sessions (cline-v2 conversations); REPL ownership may stay per process.\n122: - C6 Action types come only from `docs/context/action-types.md`; where code in this plan records a tool run it uses dialog items with category `tool_call`/`tool_result`; adding `tool_execution` needs its own requirement, doc change, and server validation first.\n123: - C7 Each decision is written as the workspace triple: a `designDecisions` entry, a dialog item with category `decision`, and a `design_decision` action.\n124: - C8 Completion: after S10 a completion without `requestClass` and terminal reviews is refused with 400 `session_turn_completion_gate`; callers treat it as a final, non-retried failure and the turn stays in progress; hooks never complete turns.\n125: - C9 Typed failures carry the server or plugin detail code (`turn_immutable`, `skipped_terminal`, `host_session_unknown`, `host_session_ambiguous`, `request_ambiguous`, `request_unknown`, `turn_logging_unsupported`, `mint_requires_host_ingress`, `nonce_source_missing`, `session_turn_completion_gate`, `request_class_invalid`, `review_*`, `ingress_nonce_invalid`) so callers can tell retryable from final failures.\n126: - C10 Review scores travel as their original text: Node never converts them to JS numbers (the D12 raw-token parser reads them as exact strings on Node 18 and later), and any event hash is computed over the original text, never over