e before text is recorded on the P0 session turn.\n433: \n434: Prompt hook, supersede, system events\n435: - TR-MCP-PLUGIN-013 (TR:1639) \"UserPromptSubmit hook opens exactly one turn per prompt\". Changes: the \"same text, in_progress, within 2 minutes\" dedupe is removed; each message event opens its turn through the server ingress mint with a nonce derived from that event (D1), so every delivery of one event gets one turn and identical prompts sent separately are separate turns, and a new prompt opens a new turn without canceling the open one. New ACs: TR-MCP-PLUGIN-013-AC001 a retried or replayed mint for one delivery opens one turn [A3]; -AC002 two separate deliveries of identical text open two turns [A3]; -AC003 a new prompt opens a new turn and leaves the prior turn in_progress [A4]; -AC004 system events open no turn [A3].\n436: - TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-013 (TEST:773). Adds: TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-013-AC001 two parallel hook processes given one recorded event payload open one turn, and two events with identical text open two [A3]; -AC002 no-cancel case [A4].\n437: - TR-MCP-PLUGIN-011 (TR:1625) \"Stop gate no-ops phantom turns and counts commits\". Changes: AC1 (system-event or zero-work in_progress turns are no-op'd) is replaced, because system events never open turns (TR-MCP-PLUGIN-013) and the stop gate now blocks on any real in_progress request turn and never calls completeTurn; AC2 (commits count) kept. New ACs: TR-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC001 blocks on in_progress request turns [A7]; -AC002 never calls completeTurn/failTurn and the auto-close at `plugin-hook.ps1:1017` is removed [A7]; -AC003 commits count toward model evidence (former AC2) [A7].\n438: - TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-011 (TEST:769). The \"no-ops a task-notification phantom turn\" case becomes \"the prompt hook never opens it\" (A3) and new cases \"blocks a real in_progress turn\" and \"never completeTurn\" (A7). New ACs: TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC001 [A3], -AC002 [A7].\n439: - FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001 (FR:2070). Changes: delete \"Supersede persists canceled.\"; AC005 drops its supersession clause; AC002 adds the non-opening hook outcomes `system-event-skipped` and `turn-open-contended`. New ACs: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001-AC006 opening a turn never persists canceled for another turn [A4]; -AC007 hook reports system-event-skipped/turn-open-contended without minting [A3].\n440: - FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002 (FR:2081). Changes: remove the \"canceled and cancelled supersede first persists may omit either field\" exception for hook supersede (server-side handling of client-supplied canceled stays); AC004 \"request drift\" rejection permits explicit targeting of a registered open turn. New AC: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC006 explicit requestId edits to a registered open turn are not drift [A4].\n441: - TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002 (TR:2695). Changes: drop \"supersede None\" from the statement and AC003; AC002 identity immutability applies per turn. New AC: TR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC004 per-turn identity binding across multiple open turns [A4].\n442: - TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002 (TEST:1142). Changes: AC001's supersession case becomes the no-cancel case; AC002's exit list adds `skipped_terminal`; \"Stop ordering\" becomes no-auto-close. New ACs: TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002-AC005 no-cancel [A4]; -AC006 skipped_terminal exit [A5]; -AC007 stop gate blocks and never closes [A7].\n443: - FR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 (FR:2360, `ac-1`). Changes: \"Superseded hook turns persist canceled with planFile and todoId None sentinels\" becomes \"Client-supplied canceled turns persist with None sentinels\" (server path kept; no hook producer). New AC: `ac-2` hooks never produce canceled turns [A4].\n444: - TR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 (TR:3261, `ac-1`). Changes: \"Plugin superseded persist stamps planFile and todoId None and uses UpsertTurn\" becomes \"Client-supplied canceled persists stamp None\". No new AC.\n445: - TEST-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001 (TEST:1355) and TEST-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-006 (TEST:1375). Changes: wording \"superseded hook persist\" becomes \"client-supplied canceled persist\"; server tests unchanged [A4 wording only].\n446: - TR-MCP-REPL-019 (TR:2427) \"Supersede preserves a server-refined turn title\". Changes: status superseded; the supersede path is deleted (TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003). Its intent (a refined title is never clobbered) moves to new AC TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003-AC005 per-turn edits never overwrite another turn's title [A4].\n447: - TR-MCP-REPL-015 (TR:2399). Changes: remove \"supersede\" from the incidental re-submit list; add the decision-list verbs and recordReview to it. New ACs: TR-MCP-REPL-015-AC001 title omitted on incidental re-submit of decision-list verbs [A6]; -AC002 recordReview never sends a title [S8].\n448: - FR-MCP-REPL-010 (FR:1951). Changes: inline AC (1) \"the active turn\" becomes \"the turn resolved by the explicit requestId override or the invocation's host-context binding (D2)\"; inline AC (3) drops \"supersede\". New structured ACs: FR-MCP-REPL-010-AC001 setTurnTitle targets an explicit requestId [A4]; -AC002 re-submits never revert titles [A4].\n449: - TEST-MCP-REPL-030 (TEST:1046) and TEST-MCP-REPL-040 (TEST:1066). Changes: remove the supersede cases; add the per-turn targeted title case. New ACs: TEST-MCP-REPL-030-AC001, TEST-MCP-REPL-040-AC001 [A4].\n450: \n451: Persist outcomes and per-turn edits\n452: - FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003 (FR:2092) \"Three session-log persist outcomes\". Changes: title becomes \"Session-log persist outcomes\"; AC001 enumerates four outcomes (primary persisted, degraded queued, failed/lost, and per-turn skipped_terminal); AC002 adds per-turn `turns[]` outcome fields; AC003 \"honored only when it matches the active turn\" becomes \"honored when it identifies the current or a registered open turn\"; statement \"appendActions refuses a request-id mismatch\" becomes \"refuses an unknown requestId\". New ACs: FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003-AC008 skipped_terminal is reported as not persisted with non-zero exit [A1 server, A5 plugin]; -AC009 explicit requestId