ithdraw at other `remove` and `popAll`) to `turn-state.yaml` in one atomic replace that also advances `appliedThroughOffset`, skipping records that start below it, exits at SessionEnd or when its host session is ended, and a second start for the same key exits immediately; `Resolve-PluginBridgeClaim` lets the prompt hook claim a matching unclaimed bridge mint under `turn-open.lock`. [A3 +A5]\n367\t- TEST-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001 Ingress mint client, turn-open lock, and system-event classifier. Tests: `SessionTurnIntegrity.Tests.ps1` Describes `IngressMint`, `SystemEvents`, `TurnOpenLock`. Validates FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC001..AC004, -AC008, -AC009, -AC010 (plugin side, including the arrival bridge and queue lifecycle), FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-002-AC001, -AC002, TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001 AC-001..AC-006. Also validates updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001-AC007 (case `SystemEvents_HookReportsSkipped_NoMint`).\n379\t- TEST-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004 McpAgent class and review fields. Tests: McpAgent.Tests `SessionLogWorkflowReviewTests`. Validates FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001-AC006 (McpAgent), TR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004 AC-001..AC-003.\n382\t- TEST-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003 Sections, client, MCP tool. Tests: `SessionLogRecordReviewToolTests`, `McpToolDescriptorParityTests` review cases, `McpErrorClassifierReviewTests`, client `SessionLogClientReviewTests` (`MockHttpHandler`), integration `SessionLogReviewControllerTests`. Validates FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC001, -AC002 (MCP and client), -AC004, TR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003 AC-001..AC-004.\n389\t- TEST-SUPPORT-023 Turn replace and section API. Tests: existing `SessionLogServiceReplaceDeleteTests` (baseline-green ac-1..ac-4 and TR ac-1, green receipt in P0), `SessionLogTurnReviewSectionTests` (S4), `SessionLogReviewControllerTests` section cases (S5). Validates FR-SUPPORT-016 `ac-1`..`ac-5`, TR-SUPPORT-CORE-016 `ac-1`..`ac-3`.\n394\t- FR-SUPPORT-016: TR-SUPPORT-CORE-016, TR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003; TEST-SUPPORT-023, TEST-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003\n406\t- FR-MCP-SES