{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_151","type":"agent_message","text":"**DISAGREE.** The plan is not ready for approval: accuracy **94/100**, completeness **86/100**, confidence **97/100**. P10 passes; P2, P3, P4, P5, P7, P8, and P9 fail; P1 and P6 remain unknown. I verified the full verdict persisted on my completed MCP reviewer turn. The final credential scan found no marker key in the 512 HV receipt files.\n\nThe seven defects are:\n\n- **F-R8-01 — arrival race** ([plan:82](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:82), [A3:573](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:573)). A prompt hook can mint before the detached bridge processes the same enqueue; the bridge then mints a second turn. The planned test covers bridge-first only. **Implementer fix:** define correlation for both orders and add concurrent and restart tests.\n- **F-R8-02 — missing host probes** ([host table:85](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:85), [P0.2:169](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:169)). P0.2 omits the table’s Copilot, Grok Bot, and classic Cline runtime checks. **Implementer fix:** add each probe, receipt, unavailable outcome, and matching TODO task.\n- **F-R8-03 — false test mappings** ([TEST records:379](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:379), [mappings:394](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:394)). Three mapping rows claim FR coverage absent from their TEST statements. **Implementer fix:** align the mapping edges and TEST statements with the ACs actually tested.\n- **F-R8-04 — missing RED cases** ([catalog:389](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:389), [S4:595](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:595)). S4 omits its catalog’s section-test class, and A3 lacks a named assertion that a contended hook mints nothing. **Implementer fix:** name and gate those tests in the catalog, allocation, and slices.\n- **F-R8-05 — incompatible smoke gate** ([D6:31](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:31), [verification:629](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:629)). D6 permits an installed host to be unsupported and write nothing; the live gate requires every installed host to write a turn and review. **Implementer fix:** use positive smoke for supported hosts and zero-mint, `turn_logging_unsupported` smoke for unsupported hosts.\n- **F-R8-06 — undefined wire outcome** ([contract:540](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:540), [A1:569](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:569)). `skipped_duplicate` has no trigger, outcome cardinality, or status/reason rule. Current `UpsertTurns` deduplicates repeated IDs within a submission, while a stored no-op is another possible meaning. **Operator decision required:** choose **A**, duplicate entries in one submission, or **B**, identical no-op against a stored turn; then specify and test both cases.\n- **F-R8-07 — handoff parity error** ([plan Risks:617](/home/sharpninja/.claude/plans/create-a-new-plan-giggly-music.md:617), [handoff:94](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/session-20261009/docs/handoffs/sessionturn-review-plan-20261009T022141Z.md:94)). The handoff says five extra filed triage IDs appear in the plan’s Risks section; they do not. **Implementer fix:** correct that claim or add the IDs and dispositions to the plan.\n\nThe full evidence, P1–P10 decisions, and persistence proof are in the [Markdown receipt](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/session-20261009/docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-plan-readiness-r8-20261009T200525Z.md) and [JSON receipt](/home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/session-20261009/docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-plan-readiness-r8-20261009T200525Z.json).\n\n=== VERDICT JSON ===\n{\"overallVerdict\":